# The encoder half of jellyfin's environment, read after /etc/default/jellyfin so
# that it wins. The drop-in that arranges the ordering is
# /etc/systemd/system/jellyfin.service.d/no-bundled-ffmpeg.conf, and it carries
# the reasoning.
#
# Empty rather than a path. With no --ffmpeg argument on the command line
# Jellyfin falls through to <EncoderAppPath> in /etc/jellyfin/encoding.xml, which
# leaves exactly one place that names the encoder. A path written here would
# outrank that file without saying so. The dashboard's "FFmpeg path" field only
# displays the path that won, because Jellyfin refuses to change EncoderAppPath
# through its API. To change the encoder, stop the service and edit that file.
#
# A separate file, rather than an edit to /etc/default/jellyfin, because that one
# is a dpkg conffile: rewriting it makes every jellyfin-server upgrade a conffile
# conflict that apt resolves by prompting or by keeping a stale copy.
JELLYFIN_FFMPEG_OPT=""
